# Python environment

When running Python, pytest, pip, or other Python tooling in the terminal, use the project venv at `/u/csh/venv/venv3.13`.

Prefer the venv interpreter directly:

```bash
/u/csh/venv/venv3.13/bin/python -m pytest -q
```

Or activate first in a shell session:

```bash
source /u/csh/venv/venv3.13/bin/activate && python -m pytest -q
```

Do not use system `/usr/bin/python3` unless the venv is unavailable.

Nexa repo root: `/u/csh/repos/Nexa`
Ampx repo root: `/u/csh/Ampx`
